	Building

Requirements
------------

The emulator needs a C11 compiler and GNU make. Nothing else.

	gcc or clang	./rvm and make test. CI uses gcc-13, gcc-14, clang-18
			and Apple clang.
	GNU make	everything
	dtc		make dtb only
	clang-format	make format and the lint workflow. LLVM 15.0.0.
	shellcheck	the lint workflow
	lcov		make coverage
	JDK 17		the APK
	Android SDK	the APK. Platform 35, build tools 35.0.0,
			NDK 27.2.12479018, CMake 3.22.1.
	Gradle 8.11.1	the APK
	debootstrap,	the Debian rootfs. Needs root and a Debian
	qemu-user-	 or Ubuntu host.
	static, e2fsprogs

Debian or Ubuntu:

	sudo apt-get install -y build-essential device-tree-compiler \
		shellcheck lcov

macOS:

	brew install make dtc shellcheck lcov llvm


The desktop build
-----------------

	make -j"$(nproc)"
	./rvm --help

That is all of it. ./rvm is about 295 KB in release mode and links only libc
and libm.

./scripts/build.sh does the same thing and also builds the DTB if dtc is
installed, then reports the binary size:

	./scripts/build.sh
	./scripts/build.sh --debug
	./scripts/build.sh --jobs 4


Modes
-----

MODE picks the optimisation and instrumentation level. Switching modes stamps
build/.mode and cleans automatically, because reusing objects from a different
mode is silent and confusing.

	release	default. -O2 -g. What CI ships.
	debug	-O0 -g3 -DRVM_DEBUG. For gdb and --trace.
	sanity	-O1 -g -fsanitize=address,undefined.

	make MODE=debug -j"$(nproc)"
	make MODE=sanity test TEST_ARGS=-v

Variables:

	CC		gcc by default. CI does make CC=clang-18.
	WERROR		WERROR=1 adds -Werror to every build, not just lint.
	TEST_ARGS	passed to the test runner, for example TEST_ARGS=-v.
	OPT		overrides the optimisation flags outright.
	EXTRA_CFLAGS	appended last, so it can override -O.
	EXTRA_LDFLAGS	same, at link time.

These are make variables, not options. make WERROR=1, never make -DWERROR=1.
Likewise make test TEST_ARGS=-v, never make test -v.


Targets
-------

	all	./rvm, the default
	test	build and run the suite
	lint	-Werror syntax pass over src and tests
	format	clang-format -i over the whole tree
	dtb	dtc -I dts -O dtb dtb/rvm.dts
	coverage clean rebuild with --coverage, then run the suite
	lib	build/librvm.a, the core without main.c
	run	./rvm -m 256 -k vmlinux -d disk.img --create-disk --stats
	clean	remove build/, ./rvm and the test binary
	help	print the target and variable list

make lint is -fsyntax-only. It is fast and it does not see warnings that only
appear once the compiler folds constants at -O2. Build the suite optimised with
-Werror as well:

	./scripts/test.sh --werror -v
	WERROR=1 ./scripts/test.sh


Tests
-----

	make test
	make test TEST_ARGS=-v
	stdbuf -o0 -e0 ./tests/rvm_tests -v

The stdbuf matters when a test crashes. Without it a SIGFPE or SIGSEGV loses
everything still in the stdout buffer and you get an empty log instead of the
name of the suite that died.

Coverage, if lcov is installed:

	./scripts/test.sh --coverage
	lcov --summary build/coverage.info


The device tree
---------------

rvm builds its FDT in C at boot, so it needs no external DTB. dtb/rvm.dts is
the same tree written out by hand, for reading and for diffing.

	make dtb
	./rvm --dump-dtb /tmp/generated.dtb
	dtc -I dtb -O dts /tmp/generated.dtb > /tmp/a
	dtc -I dtb -O dts dtb/rvm.dtb        > /tmp/b
	diff /tmp/a /tmp/b

That diff has to be empty.

Two rules for editing rvm.dts. Give interrupt controllers real labels, so
plic: plic@c000000, because dtc rejects a &plic reference to a node it cannot
label. And never write phandle = <N> by hand; dtc allocates them and rejects a
reference to a node whose phandle it did not assign.


A Debian guest
--------------

This is PLAN step 8. It needs root, about 2 GB of free memory and a route to
deb.debian.org, so it does not work in a restricted container and CI does not
attempt it.

	sudo ./tools/mkrootfs.sh --suite trixie --size 2G --out disk.img
	./tools/fetch_kernel.sh --out vmlinux
	./tools/run.sh

mkrootfs.sh installs debootstrap, qemu-user-static and e2fsprogs if they are
missing, runs debootstrap --arch=riscv64 --variant=minbase trixie under a
qemu-user-static chroot with --second-stage, swaps systemd for sysvinit-core,
sets a root password, writes an inittab with a ttyS0 getty and an fstab for
/dev/vda, /proc and /sys, then packs the tree into an ext4 image with
mke2fs -d.

fetch_kernel.sh downloads linux-image-6.12+deb13-riscv64 from the Debian pool
and extracts the uncompressed ELF vmlinux. The loader wants real ELF64 with
PT_LOAD segments, not a compressed Image and not an EFI zboot stub. Pass
--version 6.12.57-1 for an exact package.

Success is a login prompt:

	Debian GNU/Linux 13 rvm ttyS0

	rvm login:

tools/run.sh boots it. --net also sets up the TAP device, forwarding and NAT,
but it needs a build with virtio-net, which does not exist yet. --gdb runs the
emulator itself under gdb. --trace-from opens the instruction trace at a guest
PC. All three scripts document themselves with --help.


The Android APK
---------------

	cd android
	gradle --no-daemon assembleDebug
	adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk

There is no gradle-wrapper.jar in this repository, so ./gradlew does not exist.
Use a Gradle 8.11.1 on your PATH, or let CI build it; gradle/actions/setup-gradle
installs the version named in gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties.

	sdk install gradle 8.11.1

The SDK packages the build needs, in one go:

	sdkmanager --install "platform-tools" "platforms;android-35" \
		"build-tools;35.0.0" "ndk;27.2.12479018" "cmake;3.22.1"
	yes | sdkmanager --licenses

android-actions/setup-android@v3 needs those listed explicitly. Without a
packages: input it tries to install the retired tools package and fails.

The release variant is minified and resource shrunk and signed with the debug
key so it is installable without setting up a keystore. Do not publish that
artifact. Cut a real signing config first.

For reference, the debug APK is about 75 KB and the release APK about 65 KB,
against a 5 MB budget that CI enforces as a hard failure.

android/jni/CMakeLists.txt globs src/*.c with CONFIGURE_DEPENDS and drops
src/main.c, with ANDROID_STL=none and only arm64-v8a and x86_64. One copy of
the emulator, shared with the desktop build.


Continuous integration
----------------------

Five workflows in .github/workflows. All of them cache ccache or Gradle and
cancel in progress runs for the same ref.

build	push and PR to main. gcc-13, gcc-14 and clang-18 on ubuntu-24.04 plus
	Apple clang on macos-14. Runs make dtb, smoke tests --version, --help
	and --dump-dtb, and uploads rvm-linux-amd64 and rvm-macos-arm64.

test	push and PR to main. The suite under gcc-14 and clang-18 with -Werror,
	an ASan and UBSan job with halt_on_error=1 and leak detection, and an
	lcov coverage job that writes to the step summary.

lint	push and PR to main. clang-format pinned to 15.0.0 with --dry-run
	--Werror, which uploads a patch on failure. -Werror builds under both
	compilers. shellcheck -x over tools and scripts.

android	push and PR to main. Debug and release APKs, a size report, and a hard
	failure above 5 MB.

release	tag v*, or manual. A gate job runs format, lint and the tests, then
	the APK is built and published to a GitHub Release. The release has no
	body text and no generated notes, just the tag as the title.

Cut a release by tagging:

	git tag -a v0.1.0 -m "RVM 0.1.0"
	git push origin v0.1.0

A tag with a hyphen in it, v0.2.0-rc1, publishes as a pre-release.


Troubleshooting
---------------

make: invalid option -- 'D'. You wrote make -DWERROR=1. Make variables are
bare: make WERROR=1.

Mixed mode link errors. build/.mode should have caught it. Run make clean
anyway.

clang-format produces a huge diff. You are on a different LLVM major version
than 15. npx clang-format@1.8.0 fetches the right one, or use
/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin/clang-format on macOS.

dtc not found. make dtb and the DTB step of build.yml need
device-tree-compiler. The emulator does not, since it builds its FDT in C.

The test binary dies with no output. Run it under stdbuf -o0 -e0. The usual
cause is a SIGFPE from an INT64_MIN / -1 that reached the host division.

./gradlew: No such file or directory. Expected. Use gradle.

Gradle cannot resolve com.android.tools.build:aapt2. The project needs
dependencyResolutionManagement with google() and mavenCentral() in
android/settings.gradle.kts. It is there. If you removed it, put it back.
